      "title": "Sentence 3 — Challenging the Way Success Is Defined",
      "text": "**Original (J):**\n\n> If success is defined only by girls catching up with boys, disadvantaged boys may disappear from view.\n\n**Simpler paraphrase:**\n\nIf we judge success only by whether girls achieve the same results as boys, we may overlook boys who are also struggling.\n\n**Structure and grammar:**\n\nThis is a conditional sentence using a passive construction.\n\n- **Condition:** *If success is defined only by girls catching up with boys*\n- **Consequence:** *disadvantaged boys may disappear from view*\n\nThe passive *is defined* focuses attention on the method of measurement rather than on who defines it.\n\nThe expression **by + -ing** identifies the criterion used to judge success.\n\n*Disappear from view* is metaphorical: it means becoming overlooked or no longer receiving attention.\n\n**Transfer example:**\n\n> If business success is defined only by revenue growth, employee well-being may disappear from view.\n\n**Writing insight:** This structure is useful for challenging a limited definition, measurement or assumption in analytical essays.",
